up|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|In 4@H, had West bid it, partner probably leads the @SQ. So E/W lose the first trick. Then when West plays 3 rounds of hearts North wins the @HQ and has an obvious club lead. This gives N/S two additional clubs tricks for down 1. Therefore, pass by West turned out to be the best bid.|
PG| ***** 45 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^^B@2^*BMovie Maker: ^*NWe will change the bidding so West bids 4@H. Then you can play it with your friends or double dummy and see how it is done.|
