mb|P|mb|P|mb|1C|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I agree with the 1@C opener. My theory about opening at the 1-level in 3rd seat is counter to most better players. I don't believe in opening light. I will only open |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=ruleof20,Rule of 20^*N|CP||FP||at| hands. |
PG| ***** 49 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Theoretically, North does not meet the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=ruleof20,Rule of 20^*N|CP||FP||at| with only 11 HCP and 8 cards in the 2 longest suits. However I don't use HCP to do my |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=ruleof20,Rule of 20^*N|CP||FP||at| calculations. |
PG| ***** 50 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I use "Bergen adjusted points" where I use starting point rules other than length to calculate points which means I add 1 for quality suits, 1 for an abundance of aces and tens, and subtract 1 for doubleton queens/jacks or singleton kings/queens/jacks. |
PG| ***** 51 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|So on this hand North has 12 "Bergen adjusted points" because they can add 1 for the quality (3 honor) club suit meaning it meets the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=ruleof20,Rule of 20^*N|CP||FP||at|.|
PG| ***** 52 ***** |


mb|2C|mb|?|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|There is a complicated system you can play over any hand where an opponent makes a 2 suited overcall where both suits are known. In this case 2@C shows hearts and spades and the system would be on.|
PG| ***** 53 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|It is called ^*BUnusual over Unusual^*n because it most often applies over an unusual 2N where both suits are always known. It also applies over a minor suit |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=michaels,Michaels Cuebids ^*N|CP||FP||at|where both suits are also known. Having said that, I don't suggest you necessarily play it as it is a little complicated. But if you are interested there is a lesson on my web site is|CP|1|FP|2|AT| ^*Hwww.hondobridge.com^*N|FP||CP||at|.|
PG| ***** 54 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Instead, I suggest you use a cue bid to show a limit raise. Here if I bid 3@C that is weak. In this auction a cue bid means 2@H or 2@S since they are both suits that East is known to have.|
PG| ***** 55 ***** |


mb|3C|an|less than limit raise|
pg| ***** 56 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^^B@2^*BWest: ^*NWhy didn't you bid 2@H ?|
PG| ***** 57 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^^
^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Because I have less than a limit raise.|
PG| ***** 58 ***** |


mb|3H|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I would play 3@H by West is not strong per se and I am not sure I would bid 3@H with the West hand. It just should show 4 hearts. On the other hand, West had a problem and 3@H is better than the other less appealing bids.|
PG| ***** 59 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Another possibility is for East to double, which should be a "Responsive Double" asking West to bid their better major. But with an unfamiliar partner, I would worry that partner would think it was a penalty double, so choosing the less ambiguous 3@H bid has merit.|
PG| ***** 60 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|P?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Although East has 12 HCP and West freely bid 3@H, since the @CK is probably a wasted card and East's spades are very weak, East should pass.|
PG| ***** 61 ***** |


mb|P|
pg| ***** 62 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|
pc|CA|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Although normally I don't like leading unprotected aces, on this auction I think the @CA is possible because partner opened 1@C and I showed a weak limit raise. If I didn't lead the @CA I would lead a diamond.|
PG| ***** 63 ***** |


pc|CK|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Because dummy has a singleton, my club spot is now suit preference. A high club spot means to lead a spade. A low club spot means lead a diamond. So after I play my @C9 it tells partner to lead a spade.|
